    <description>[BMS46 v0.50 CODE-DERIVED] PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_015E00 is called only from set_Engine_Timing_Advance. In its normal branch it compares Engine_Load FF837C with 0xA49F, together with the adjacent RPM threshold 0xA4A0, to select one of four calibration pairs controlling the up/down slew of the timing-advance state. Engine_Load scaling is established as 0.715 kg/h per bit. Q28G raw 66 -&gt; 47.190 kg/h. 0xA4A0 has only one direct xref and remains for the later exhaustiveness pass. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
