    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_02414A, the 16-bit word at 0x95F4 is loaded, shifted left by 8 and compared against both positive and negative magnitude of the transient delta state D4; exceeding +/- this threshold sets state bit 0x40. Q28G word 0x0001 therefore represents an effective comparison threshold of 256 internal Q8 counts. Motorola/MSB-first word order is used. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
