    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452 forms an RPM-derived idle reference term from 0x8894 * Engine_RPM_Diagnostic_Word FF8338 &gt;&gt; 8 and caps that 16-bit result at 0x8896 before it is combined with the idle RPM target state. FF8338 is the same RPM word whose high byte is FF8334 (40 RPM/bit), giving 40/256 = 0.15625 RPM per word count. Q28G word 0x3000 = 12288 -&gt; 1920 RPM. Motorola/MSB-first word order is used. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
