    <description>[BMS46 v0.51 CODE-DERIVED] In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_016452, the low-voltage idle state is entered when Engine_Alternator is below 0x889B under the required idle/stationary conditions. While that state bit is active, 0x8898 is shifted left by 6 and supplied as the target to the state slew function for FF8438. Because FF8338/64 is RPM/10 in the same logic, this byte is a 10-RPM-per-bit target. Q28G raw 84 -&gt; 840 RPM. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
