  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x285">
    <title>Lambda State LowBand Transition Disable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED] Bit0 of calibration byte 0x92C3. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01DF34, when this bit is SET the low-band lambda-state transition that would set runtime bit1 is inhibited. Stock 0x92C3=0xFC, so bit0 is CLEAR and the transition is permitted. TunerPro flag editing changes only mask 0x01 and preserves bits1..7. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="0" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x92C3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x286">
    <title>Lambda State HighBand Transition Disable</title>
    <description>[BMS46 v0.68 MASK-PRESERVING FLAG / CODE-DERIVED] Bit1 of calibration byte 0x92C3. In PROVISIONAL_CAL_CONSUMER_01DF34, when this bit is SET the high-band lambda-state transition that would set runtime bit2 is inhibited. Stock 0x92C3=0xFC, so bit1 is CLEAR and the transition is permitted. TunerPro flag editing changes only mask 0x02 and preserves bits0 and2..7. | R3 EXTENDED: full-v1.09-derived scalar/flag outside canonical legacy map spans.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="0" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x92C3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x02</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
